                        "review": "interesting aesthetic, but feels unfinished. this game caught my attention with its weird cyberpunk style and atmosphere, but actually playing it was rough. A lot of the mechanics feel half-baked, progression gets repetitive fast, and the combat/gameplay never really evolves into anything interesting.\n\nThere’s some charm in the presentation, but clunky controls and technical issues made it hard for me to stay invested. It feels less like a fully polished game and more like an experimental project that needed a lot more time in development.",
